stdpopsim — GPL-3.0-or-later, and why it is not installed by default
--------------------------------------------------------------------

stdpopsim (PopSim Consortium) is GPL-3.0-or-later. It was pinned in
`requirements.txt` until 2026-08-15, which meant `make setup` placed GPLv3
code into the default environment of a project whose LICENSE says
Apache-2.0.

Those licences are compatible in one direction only. Apache-2.0 code may be
taken into a GPLv3 work; GPLv3 code cannot be folded into a work
distributed under Apache-2.0 without the combination becoming GPLv3.

Nothing was being violated — Caterva never bundled stdpopsim, and running
two separately-installed packages together on your own machine is use, not
distribution. But a reader would have had to compare two licence files and
reason about their interaction to work out what they had, and this project's
central claim is that nothing should require that.

It now lives in `requirements-popgen.txt` and is opt-in. The code already
worked this way: `Tests/popgen_resolver.py` wraps `import stdpopsim` in
try/except ImportError and returns `found=False` with a search log saying
so. The manifest was the only thing claiming it was required.

See docs/adr/0061-gpl-out-of-the-default-install.md.


