      fetches live. Each page is listed with its URL, fetch date and hash in
      Tests/fixtures/recorded/README.md.

  docs/literature-inventory.toml
      Golden-tuple entries recording BRENDA values and reference ids, e.g.
      the LDH/lactate Km (ref 740253) and the LDH/gossypol Ki (ref 711801).

  Tests/, Science-Agent-Pipeline/artifacts/api-server/src/
      BRENDA reference ids used as test expectations and citation fixtures.

MODIFICATIONS

CC BY 4.0 §3(a)(1)(B) requires that modifications be indicated. Caterva
does modify the data it extracts:

  * rows are filtered by organism and substrate
  * units are normalised and re-labelled
  * values whose source does not report assay pH and temperature are
    FLAGGED as incomplete under the STRENDA Guidelines rather than
    presented as verified
  * the HTML fixtures in Tests/fixtures/ are trimmed excerpts of full
    BRENDA pages, not complete copies (the recorded pages in
    Tests/fixtures/recorded/ are complete and unmodified)

The underlying measurements are unaltered. Caterva never edits a value.

NO WARRANTY

CC BY 4.0 §5: the Licensed Material is offered as-is and as-available, and
the licensor makes no representations or warranties of any kind concerning
it. Caterva restates that disclaimer here and extends it: a value resolved
through Caterva carries whatever uncertainty the original measurement
carried, and Caterva's provenance reporting does not make a measurement
more reliable than it was.

CITATION

If you use BRENDA data in scientific work, cite BRENDA's current
publication — see https://www.brenda-enzymes.org/references.php. Citing
