ExPASy ENZYME — the enzyme nomenclature
---------------------------------------

`caterva/enzymes/data/enzyme_index.json.gz` is derived from the ENZYME
nomenclature database (https://enzyme.expasy.org/), which distributes the
IUBMB enzyme nomenclature. It is copyrighted by the SIB Swiss Institute of
Bioinformatics and distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
The release the index was built from, "Release of 02-Sep-2026", is recorded
inside the index and in `caterva/enzymes/data/NOTICE.txt`.

Creator: the SIB Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics (ExPASy ENZYME database, Bridge and Axelsen), which distributes the IUBMB enzyme nomenclature.

MODIFICATIONS (CC BY 4.0 §3(a)(1)(B)). Caterva reduced the two files
`enzyme.dat` and `enzclass.txt` to accepted names, alternative names,
reactions, status (active, transferred with the new number, or deleted),
enzyme-class names and the UniProt entry names listed per EC number. The
comment lines are dropped. UniProt entries are kept as a count per organism
and, in full, for 13 organisms. `scripts/build_enzyme_index.py` does this,
